#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092217 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092059 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f65d032-9acc-5fe6-b7c2-b8293576cb4c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Given in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "bc48e845-b2a7-5e30-9c73-b7d842f4090c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5383" :question/problem "The point $P$ has polar coordinates $\\left( 6,\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\right).$ Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P.$" :question/worked-solution "To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx = r\\cos\\theta, \\qquad y=r\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tx &= r\\cos\\theta\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2}\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 3\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\ty &= r\\sin\\theta\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\cdot \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 3\\sqrt{3}\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $\\left(3, 3\\sqrt{3}\\right).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f65d032-9acc-5fe6-b7c2-b8293576cb4c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048292} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048465}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535409 :question-generator/id #uuid "1fb29c3f-43c5-559f-aace-7e2c309d2d42" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186092217.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f65d032-9acc-5fe6-b7c2-b8293576cb4c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Given in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5754374-bb37-57a0-9738-e72c3a15a78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/mat