\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =7\\cdot -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-\\frac{7}{2},-\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{2}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f65d032-9acc-5fe6-b7c2-b8293576cb4c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Given in Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3aed14ab-8d46-5a5a-b69e-54ab7aa8f694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{9}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535361} {:answer/id #uuid "be98640b-fc34-541e-98d6-49a473e3cb90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{9}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535389} {:answer/id #uuid "db60710d-3e09-597c-b11b-2bc72d8b9f23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{9}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535396} {:answer/id #uuid "e3accfff-2b68-51b9-bb29-d90c582a9cc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535400} {:answer/id #uuid "f163e33c-08cc-5022-b584-22b7982a8577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{9}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535406}] :answer-field/correct {:answe